            <ArticleTitle>Will coronary artery surgery disappear in 10 years' time?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>747-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Over the past 20 years, percutaneous coronary intervention has progressively developed and matured, and many patients with severe coronary artery disease can now be revascularized non-surgically. So are the days of coronary artery bypass graft surgery numbered?</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
